- op: discuss  # b9ba
  at: '2026-03-30T22:03:48Z'  # b9ba
  by: agent  # b9ba
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b9ba
  clock: 35  # b9ba
  nonce: b9ba  # b9ba
  message: "Great question. Yes — the remaining issues (Spring class-level @RequestMapping chaining, Express middleware paths) are better addressed through the framework pattern YAML system than analyzer-specific code changes.\n\nThe framework YAML patterns already support 'enrichment' rules that extract metadata from annotations. What's missing is a 'path composition' concept: the ability to declare that a class-level annotation provides a prefix that should be prepended to method-level paths. For example:\n\n```yaml\n# Hypothetical spring.yaml addition\npath_composition:\n  - class_annotation: RequestMapping\n    method_annotations: [GetMapping, PostMapping, PutMapping, DeleteMapping, PatchMapping]\n    compose: '{class_path}/{method_path}'\n```\n\nThis would be a framework_patterns.py enhancement, not a Java analyzer change. Similarly, Express middleware could be declared:\n\n```yaml\nmiddleware_routes:\n  - pattern: app.use\n    path: '*'\n    kind: middleware_route\n```\n\nThis approach is more modular, reusable (same mechanism works for JAX-RS, Spring, Micronaut, Quarkus), and doesn't require touching analyzer code. The implementation would go in framework_patterns.py's route materialization phase."  # b9ba
